Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the VADC using an incorrect reference voltage (1.25V) for channel calibration of the temperature channels instead of the correct VDD reference (1.875V). This misconfiguration likely led to inaccurate temperature readings being reported to the thermal framework. Additionally, the lack of a proper delay between AMUX configuration and ADC conversion could have further contributed to the inaccuracies in the readings.

